        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(apps): add native mobile Automations parity",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe web Control UI can manage scheduled gateway work, while the native mobile apps exposed only a partial cron surface. iOS lacked safe detail/edit/history/run/delete controls, and both mobile platforms lacked practical search and status filtering.\n\nCloses #106145.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Use the existing `cron.*` gateway contract; no new protocol or config surface.\n- Add mobile-appropriate management parity while keeping creation, cloning, and dense delivery/failure-routing editing in the Control UI.\n- Preserve optimistic-concurrency safety with `expectedConfigRevision` and fail closed when the connected gateway changes.\n- Track queued runs by exact `runId`, paginate the complete automation list, and preserve unsaved drafts.\n- Fold in the outstanding native Skills review fixes from #105814.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- iOS and Android now call the feature **Automations**.\n- Both apps support search plus All / Active / Paused filters.\n- iOS adds configuration detail, recent history, revision-safe editing, enable/pause, Run Now tracking, and confirmed deletion.\n- Android retains its existing management surface with the same product naming and discovery controls.\n- Create/clone and advanced delivery/failure routing remain available in the web Control UI.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Android focused unit tests: Cron management/runtime, Settings filters, and Skills management.\n- iOS focused tests: 10 Automations model/revision/pagination/outcome tests passed on iPhone 17 Pro / iOS 26.5.\n- OpenClawKit focused tests: 9 Skills management tests passed.\n- Native screenshot XCUITests: Automations and Skills screens passed on iPhone 17 Pro / iOS 26.5.\n- Android source-blind behavior pass: navigation, search empty state, Active/Paused filtering, detail configuration, and management actions.\n- Native localization: 4,482 source entries synchronized across all 21 locale artifacts.\n- Screenshots posted below.\n\nAgent-assisted implementation; sanitized transcript omitted because no transcript attachment was requested.\n",
